Multics mail message #15, from a lineprinter listing of mail received by
Lippard.Scouting.  Transcribed verbatim from the accompanying photograph
explore.mail.1980-08-13.jpeg; line breaks, spacing and punctuation are as
printed.  The listing page also carries an unrelated message #14, which is
not reproduced here.


#15 (10 lines)  08/13/80 18:34  Mailed by: Lippard.Scouting
Date:  13 August 1980 18:12 mst
From:  Akers.SCUdmp
Subject: explore
To:  Lippard.sct
cc:  Perrine.sct
Acknowledge-To:  Akers.SCUdmp

Although I know that version 6.1 is no longer supported, I don't know if
you found this bug in some prior version and fixed it for 7.0 or not.
The bug:

If in the cellar of the shack, one attempts to go north, one suddenly
finds himself once again at the edge of the clearing (at least this
happens with the flashlight off.) If the flashlight is on, it tells you
that there is no way to go that direction.

                                        -- Scott, the vagabond --

---(15)---
